{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_14a5889d", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T13:02:00", "text": "Great find, Julia! I'll check out their solution and see if we can adapt any techniques for handling skewed data in our algorithm. 📊", "utterranceID": "20260804-4-352ab"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260804-4-352ab"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fa16fefb", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T13:05:00", "text": "Lastly, there's a bug in Apache Spark titled 'Data Processing Bottleneck with Large Datasets'. It talks about delays during data aggregation tasks. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/5198. David, this seems relevant to the bottleneck issue you're tackling.", "utterranceID": "20260804-5-1ab45"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260804-5-1ab45"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2542cff3", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T13:08:00", "text": "Thanks, Julia! I'll dive into their PR to see how they optimized their data processing pipeline. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260804-6-c1f2d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260804-6-c1f2d"}
