{"title": "Update Security Module to Use Modern Encryption Algorithm", "summary": "This pull request addresses the issue of improper data encryption in collaborative discussions. The root cause was identified as the use of an outdated encryption algorithm in the security module, which was vulnerable to known exploits. 

To resolve this, the encryption algorithm has been updated to a modern, secure standard that ensures data is properly encrypted in transit. The changes include:
- Replacing the outdated algorithm with AES-256 encryption.
- Updating relevant documentation to reflect the changes.

The fix was tested by:
- Conducting unit tests to verify the encryption and decryption processes.
- Performing integration tests to ensure data is securely transmitted and received in collaborative discussions.
- Running security audits to confirm the elimination of vulnerabilities.

These changes ensure that sensitive data is now securely encrypted, protecting it from unauthorized access.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/CollaborateForce/pull/63", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "63", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_8986ddc3"}, "created_at": "2027-03-01T22:40:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_131494b8"}, "comment": "The changes look great! The update to AES-256 encryption effectively addresses the vulnerability. I've reviewed the code and tested the implementation, and everything is functioning as expected. Approved for merge.", "submitted_at": "2027-03-01T21:46:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_CollaborateForce_pull_63"}

