{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidgarcia-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-force-d1c875"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bd791efc", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T23:28:00", "text": "Hi team, I've found some interesting parallels in open-source projects that might help us with our current Salesforce issues. Let's take a look! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261027-0-ef158"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-0-ef158"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidgarcia-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-force-d1c875"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bd791efc", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T23:32:00", "text": "First, there's a 'Memory Leak in Model Training' issue in TensorFlow. It's about excessive memory consumption during model training with large datasets, leading to crashes and slow performance. Sounds familiar, right? Here's the PR link: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/1296. @eid_57e922c4, this might give us some insights for the memory leak in our visualization engine.", "utterranceID": "20261027-1-de4ae"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-1-de4ae"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidgarcia-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-force-d1c875"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_57e922c4", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T23:37:00", "text": "Thanks, David! I'll definitely check out the TensorFlow PR. It could offer some valuable strategies for optimizing memory usage in our case. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261027-2-646af"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-2-646af"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidgarcia-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-force-d1c875"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bd791efc", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T23:42:00", "text": "Next up, we have an 'Inefficient Data Caching Strategy' in Apache Spark. The issue is about a suboptimal caching mechanism causing delays in data processing and retrieval, which affects performance in large-scale data operations. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/1297. Alice, this seems quite similar to our data caching issue.", "utterranceID": "20261027-3-59848"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-3-59848"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a8040636", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:30:00", "text": "I agree with David M. The JupyterLab approach seems user-friendly and intuitive. We should consider how they handle the UI/UX aspects, especially the resizing functionality. @eid_446bc3ee, maybe you could look into how they implemented it?", "utterranceID": "20260618-3-653be"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-3-653be"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:34:00", "text": "Great points, David and David! I'll definitely take a closer look at their implementation. Next, let's talk about Grafana's Dashboard Panel Customization Options. This feature introduces customization for dashboard panels, allowing users to adjust size and visibility. Here's the link: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/3251. Thoughts? @eid_13df35ed", "utterranceID": "20260618-4-c88c0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-4-c88c0"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13df35ed", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:37:00", "text": "Grafana's feature is quite comprehensive. Their focus on dashboard panels is similar to our widgets. I like how they provide a seamless experience for users to personalize their dashboards. We should consider their approach to user interaction and settings management.", "utterranceID": "20260618-5-34952"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-5-34952"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:41:00", "text": "Absolutely, George! Grafana's user interaction model could be very beneficial for us. Lastly, let's look at Kibana's Customizable Visualization Panels. This feature adds options for modifying the size and visibility of visualization panels on dashboards. Check it out here: https://github.com/elastic/kibana/pull/3252. What do you think, team?", "utterranceID": "20260618-6-37673"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-6-37673"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_76d9cb07", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:42:00", "text": "Kibana's feature is quite similar to Grafana's, but I think their focus on visualization panels could offer us some unique insights, especially in terms of data representation and user control. We should definitely consider their approach.", "utterranceID": "20260618-7-c9bfa"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-7-c9bfa"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a8040636", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:44:00", "text": "Agreed, David M. Kibana's emphasis on visualization is something we can learn from. It might be worth exploring how they handle data-heavy widgets and ensure performance isn't compromised. @eid_446bc3ee, could you look into this as well?", "utterranceID": "20260618-8-432e1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-8-432e1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-06-18T14:47:00", "text": "Definitely, I'll dig deeper into both Grafana and Kibana's implementations. Thanks for the input, everyone! I'll compile my findings and we can discuss how to adapt these ideas for our feature. Let's keep the creativity flowing! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260618-9-31229"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260618-9-31229"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-06-19T15:59:00", "text": "Hi team, please check my PR for adding customization options to the dashboard widgets: https://github.com/salesforce/ghtAIX/pull/17. This update allows users to resize widgets by dragging their edges, toggle visibility, and ensures changes persist across sessions. Let me know your thoughts! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260621-0-1ca5a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260621-0-1ca5a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgegarcia-InsightForce", "channelID": "ch-htaix-cd6571"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_76d9cb07", "timestamp": "2026-06-19T16:00:00", "text": "Hey @eid_446bc3ee, just took a quick look at the PR. The resizing feature is really smooth! I'll dive deeper into the code now. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260621-1-2e870"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260621-1-2e870"}

{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_719a0253", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:22:00", "text": "Hi team, I've shared the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/knowledgeforce_technical_specifications_document|Technical Specifications Document> for KnowledgeForce. Let's discuss any feedback or suggestions you might have. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260617-0-0e8cb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-0-0e8cb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_52681a26", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:26:00", "text": "Thanks, Hannah! @eid_719a0253. I noticed in the System Architecture section, you mention using BERT and GPT for NLP tasks. Could we specify which versions we're using? This might help clarify the capabilities we're leveraging.", "utterranceID": "20260617-1-19ef1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-1-19ef1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_97b4acd0", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:29:00", "text": "Good point, Fiona. Also, in the Data Privacy and Security section, could we elaborate more on the role-based access controls? Maybe provide examples of roles and their access levels? This could help in understanding our security measures better.", "utterranceID": "20260617-2-91b49"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-2-91b49"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2c384d22", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:34:00", "text": "I agree with Julia. Additionally, in the Integration and Interfaces section, it might be beneficial to list some of the CRM systems and databases we support for data ingestion. This could give potential clients a clearer picture of compatibility.", "utterranceID": "20260617-3-4a32b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-3-4a32b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fa16fefb", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:35:00", "text": "Hey @eid_719a0253, I think the Competitive Analysis section could use a bit more depth. Maybe we could add a table comparing key features with IBM Watson and Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services? This could highlight our strengths more effectively.", "utterranceID": "20260617-4-b2e68"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-4-b2e68"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9937f1d5", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:37:00", "text": "I like that idea, Julia. Also, in the Strategic Initiatives and Future Developments section, could we add a timeline for the blockchain integration and self-service analytics module? It would be great to set some expectations there.", "utterranceID": "20260617-5-523dc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-5-523dc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_072d9c10", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:42:00", "text": "I noticed that the User Interface and Experience section mentions customizable dashboards. Could we include a screenshot or a mock-up? Visuals might help convey the design and functionality better.", "utterranceID": "20260617-6-b9a15"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-6-b9a15"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_719a0253", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:44:00", "text": "Thanks for all the feedback, everyone! 😊 To summarize: \n- Specify versions of BERT and GPT in System Architecture.\n- Elaborate on role-based access controls with examples.\n- List supported CRM systems and databases.\n- Add a comparison table in Competitive Analysis.\n- Include a timeline for future developments.\n- Consider adding visuals for the UI section.\n\nI'll make these updates and share a revised draft soon. Any other thoughts? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260617-7-7b669"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-7-7b669"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-geaix-c41fb2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_82e9fcef", "timestamp": "2026-06-17T23:46:00", "text": "That sounds great, Hannah. Just one more thing, in the Machine Learning and Algorithms section, could we mention any plans for continuous model updates or improvements? It might be reassuring for clients to know we're committed to keeping our models up-to-date.", "utterranceID": "20260617-8-4bb9c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260617-8-4bb9c"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-310592"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6aaf9156", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T04:55:00", "text": "Finally, there's Metabase's Custom Query Builder Interface. It adds a new interface for building custom queries with drag-and-drop functionality. Here's the link: https://github.com/metabase/metabase/pull/3378. What do you think, team?", "utterranceID": "20260703-7-0e811"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260703-7-0e811"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-310592"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8b95a6f0", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T05:00:00", "text": "The drag-and-drop query builder is a fantastic idea! It could make complex query building much more accessible to non-technical users. We should definitely explore this further. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260703-8-957c2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260703-8-957c2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-310592"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_524f697b", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T05:02:00", "text": "Agreed, Alice! This could be a game-changer for user engagement. It might be a bit challenging to implement, but the payoff could be huge. Maybe we can prioritize this feature after the initial dashboard setup?", "utterranceID": "20260703-9-f9b01"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260703-9-f9b01"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-310592"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6aaf9156", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T05:04:00", "text": "Awesome insights, everyone! I'll take a closer look at these features and see how we can adapt them for our dashboard. Let's keep the conversation going as we move forward. Thanks for the input! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260703-10-ffefa"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260703-10-ffefa"}
